  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\u03a0$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=\u27e8-1,-2,6\u27e9+t\u27e82,5,4\u27e9,\\,\u03a0:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e8-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ \u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81,2,1\u27e9 & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e81,2,1\u27e9 & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e8-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e81,2,1\u27e9 & =33 \\\\ \u27e8-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81,2,1\u27e9 & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e8-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,8,14\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$",
